WHAT: normalizeLocale assumes the locale contains a '-' separator and dereferences parts[1].toUpperCase() (line 13) even when the input has none. WHY: updateProfile passes the raw client body to checkProfileFields, and locale is only type-checked as a string, so a request like POST { "locale": "en" } makes parts[1] undefined and throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'toUpperCase')`, returning an unhandled 500 instead of a validation error. HOW: guard the split result and treat a missing region as unsupported, e.g.

const parts = input.replace('_', '-').split('-');
if (parts.length !== 2 || !parts[0] || !parts[1]) {
    throw new HttpError(400, `unsupported locale ${input}`);
}
return `${parts[0].toLowerCase()}-${parts[1].toUpperCase()}`;

WHAT: The new scope.All branch filters refs with `if r.Final`, marking only final refs live, so non-final refs (builds still uploading) are treated as dead. WHY: A build that is still uploading has a non-final ref whose blob then appears unreferenced; Sweep with Scope{All:true} lists all blobs (sweep.go:18-21 sets project="") and deletes that blob, so when the build finalizes its ref points at a blob that no longer exists — data loss. This contradicts the invariant the sibling ByProject loop states at live.go:45-48 ("Non-final refs belong to builds still uploading: their blobs stay"). HOW: drop the Final check and mark every ref digest live, matching the non-All branch:
	for _, r := range refs {
		live[r.Digest] = true
	}
